  "body": "Currently we pretend that all `CharacterData` nodes (`Text`, `CDATASection`, `ProcessingInstruction`, and `Comment`) can have infinite length. In practice however it seems the upper limit has to be JavaScript's `String`'s maximum length, which is 2<sup>53</sup> &minus; 1.\n\nShould we standardize on that and attempt to deal with the consequences for `wholeText`, `normalize()`, etc?\n\ncc @rniwa @smaug---- @mfreed7 ",
